## Dandelion-like nickel/cobalt metal-organic framework based electrode materials for high performance supercapacitors
Shuwen Gao, Yanwei Sui, Fuxiang Wei, Jiqiu Qi, Qingkun Meng, Yaojian Ren, Yezeng He
School of Materials Science and Engineering, China University of Mining and Technology, Xuzhou 221116, People's Republic of China
G R A P H I C A L A B S T R A C T
## A R T I C L E I N F O
Article history:  Received 19 May 2018  Revised 10 July 2018  Accepted 12 July 2018
Keywords:  Ni-MOF  Ni/Co-MOF  Supercapacitors
## A B S T R A C T
Metal-organic frameworks (MOFs), serving as a promising electrode material in the supercapacitors, have attracted tremendous interests in recent years. Here, through modifying the molar ratio of the \(\mathrm{Ni}^{2+}\) and \(\mathrm{Co}^{2+}\), we have successfully fabricated Ni-MOF and Ni/Co-MOF by a facile hydrothermal method. The Ni/Co-MOF with a dandelion-like hollow structure shows an excellent specific capacitance of \(758\;\mathrm{F}\;\mathrm{g}^{-1}\) at \(1\;\mathrm{A}\;\mathrm{g}^{-1}\) in the three-electrode system. Comparing with Ni-MOF, the obtained Ni/Co-MOF has a better rate capacitance (89% retention at \(10\;\mathrm{A}\;\mathrm{g}^{-1}\)) and cycling life (75% retention after 5000 circulations). Besides, the assembled asymmetric supercapacitor based on Ni/Co-MOF and active carbon exhibits a high specific energy density of \(20.9\;\mathrm{W}\,\mathrm{h}\,\mathrm{kg}^{-1}\) at the power density of \(800\;\mathrm{W}\,\mathrm{kg}^{-1}\). All these results demonstrate that the mixed-metal strategy is an effective way to optimize the morphology and improve the electrochemical property of the MOFs.
